<article class="env-lemma" id="08Z5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08Z5">Lemma <span data-tag="08Z5">47.7.4</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a flat local homomorphism of local Noetherian rings such that $R/\mathfrak m_ R \cong S/\mathfrak m_ R S$. Then the injective hull of the residue field of $R$ is the injective hull of the residue field of $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $\mathfrak m_ RS = \mathfrak m_ S$ as the quotient by the former is a field. Set $\kappa = R/\mathfrak m_ R = S/\mathfrak m_ S$. Let $E_ R$ be the injective hull of $\kappa $ over $R$. Let $E_ S$ be the injective hull of $\kappa $ over $S$. Observe that $E_ S$ is an injective $R$-module by Lemma <a href="/tag/08XQ" data-tag="08XQ">47.3.2</a>. Choose an extension $E_ R \to E_ S$ of the identification of residue fields. This map is an isomorphism by Lemma <a href="/tag/08Z4" data-tag="08Z4">47.7.3</a> because $R \to S$ induces an isomorphism $R/\mathfrak m_ R^ n \to S/\mathfrak m_ S^ n$ for all $n$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>